<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Ewart Gladstone</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1809">1809</a>–<a href="/years/1898">1898</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Ewart Gladstone was a British Liberal statesman who served four times as prime minister between 1868 and 1894. His governments introduced the secret ballot, state elementary education, army reform and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/representation-of-the-people-act-1884">Third Reform Act</a>, disestablished the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-ireland">Church of Ireland</a>, and in 1886 and 1893 tried without success to pass Home Rule for Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-ewart-gladstone.jpg" alt="William Ewart Gladstone" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samuel Alexander Walker · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Ewart_Gladstone,_1892_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
